ncies, competing capacity failures, compaction tampering, authority promotion, replay divergence, stale bindings, and restart/resume equivalence;\n- negative proof mutations demonstrate the contracts reject incorrect selection, omission, ordering, replacement, or replay;\n- strict no-cheating Verus, ordinary tests, strict Clippy, formatting, rustdoc, architecture, ordinary API, generated artifact, and relevant durability tests pass;\n- final source is frozen and independently reviewed with source-bound evidence before proof-impact reconciliation and hosted CI.\n\nOut of scope: cryptographic execution, clocks, storage durability itself, and external/provider effects belong to GAP-06; broader kernel/agent/protocol lifecycle composition belongs to GAP-05. Do not weaken existing checks, wire compatibility, or maintainer self-merge.\n\nDependency: GAP-03 / Crosslink issue #77 must land first so the implementation branch can be based on its protected develop result.","priority":"high","parent_uuid":"eb5c64d1-b12e-4ec5-8bae-6c66adc80c81","created_by":"oF4J"},"signed_by":"SHA256:6i1eQ/7kGjVq4DI4yUCBFk4bwyvvZOhSsWcR9SkdFok","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg/EnEj+fMMglOKHVSgF9XkfkH9og9l/fzQpIgYx0ARh4AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOiaWci9vSPW8179FxQE2rm9ry5c5kmcQjNb4qkzuacuJIdF+wiiiscHEM/1PeqcS1oKmk78jNlbeBTlizD0uwA="}
